On Mon, 19 Dec 2005, Raisse the Thaumaturge wrote:
> NunYa Bidness wrote:
>>  I wonder if one could place said scroll(s) in a corner, and throw
>> a potion of water (clear potion) on them to blank them... Hmmm...
>
> No, you can't; that is, you can throw the water, but the bottle will
> break without blanking the scrolls.

Well, we've fixed that glitch. ;)  The following patch causes a thrown
potion of water to have an effect on scrolls and rustable items in the
square where it shatters, just as if you'd dipped all those items into
the potion.
   Well, okay, there's a 1/2 chance that a rustable item won't rust, and
a 1/3 chance that a scroll won't blank. Just for balance, y'know...
   Also, this patch duplicates the current bug in which you can happily
rust away a shopkeeper's whole inventory without him getting mad at you
or charging you for the damage. Scroll-blanking costs money, though,
as it should.
   The next step, I guess, is to make thrown potions of acid do corrosion 
damage. (And oil repair it?) But those wouldn't really have any useful 
in-game effect, except to be Yet Another reason to avoiding fighting in 
shops.

   Sorry about the incredibly long lines in what follows...

-Arthur


diff -Bb nethack-3.4.3/src/dothrow.c nethack-patched/src/dothrow.c
1585a1586,1623
>
>                         /* Throwing water on scrolls and metal has an effect. */
